---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="header-inner">
      <div class="brand">
        <div class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">🌙</div>
        <h1>Derrp Studio <small>Household Command Center</small></h1>
      </div>
      <nav class="main-nav" id="mainNav" aria-label="Modules">
        <button class="nav-btn active" data-module="copy">Copy Studio</button>
        <button class="nav-btn" data-module="mochi">Mochi &amp; Sessions</button>
        <button class="nav-btn" data-module="planner">Week Planner</button>
        <button class="nav-btn" data-module="queue">Queue &amp; Prompts</button>
        <button class="nav-btn" data-module="commissions">Commission Prep</button>
        <button class="nav-btn" data-module="promo">Promo &amp; Social</button>
        <button class="nav-btn" data-module="companion">Companion</button>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="wrap">
    <!-- Status strip: computed from the household pattern in America/New_York -->
    <section class="status-strip" aria-label="Household status">
      <div class="status-cell">
        <div class="k">Tonight</div>
        <div class="v" id="stripTonight">—</div>
        <div class="s" id="stripTonightSub">Loading the household pattern…</div>
      </div>
      <div class="status-cell">
        <div class="k">Next up</div>
        <div class="v" id="stripNext">—</div>
        <div class="s" id="stripNextSub">—</div>
      </div>
      <div class="status-cell">
        <div class="k">Mochi bridge</div>
        <div class="v" id="stripBridge">Not connected</div>
        <div class="s" id="stripBridgeSub">Configure a host profile under Mochi &amp; Sessions.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ COPY STUDIO ============ -->
    <section class="module active" id="module-copy">
      <div class="grid two">
        <div class="card">
          <h2>Copy Studio</h2>
          <p class="lede">Build the full copy set for a stream. Standards are enforced as you type; drafts save to this browser.</p>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Creator</span>
            <select id="csCreator">
              <option value="neo">Neo — NeoDerrp</option>
              <option value="ama">Ama — AmaDerrp</option>
              <option value="duo">Duo — Neo + Ama</option>
            </select>
          </label>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Series</span>
            <select id="csSeries"></select>
          </label>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Hook (verb-first)</span>
            <input type="text" id="csHook" placeholder="e.g. Surviving the first boss with zero heals" />
            <span class="count" id="csHookCount"></span>
          </label>

          <label class="field">
            <span id="csGameLabel">Game / Project</span>
            <input type="text" id="csGame" placeholder="Exact Twitch category name or art project" />
          </label>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Category</span>
            <input type="text" id="csCategory" placeholder="Exact Twitch category (e.g. Metaphor: ReFantazio, Art)" />
          </label>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Last time (optional — recap-led openers for MQM / UB)</span>
            <input type="text" id="csLastTime" placeholder="One line: where the last stream left off" />
          </label>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Discord invite link (used only when cross-posting)</span>
            <input type="url" id="csInvite" value="https://discord.gg/pVPFG475Y7" />
          </label>
          <label class="switch">
            <input type="checkbox" id="csCrossPost" />
            Cross-posting (include the invite link in the Discord post)
          </label>

          <h3>Save draft</h3>
          <div class="row">
            <input type="text" id="csDraftName" class="grow" placeholder="Draft name" />
            <button class="btn" id="csSaveDraft">Save draft</button>
          </div>
          <ul class="list" id="csDraftList"></ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>Generated copy</h2>
          <p class="lede">Updates live. Welcome text is kept TTS-safe: plain text only, no emoji, links, or markdown.</p>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Twitch title</span>
            <textarea id="outTitle" rows="2"></textarea>
            <span class="count" id="outTitleCount"></span>
          </label>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Go-live message (≤ 90 chars)</span>
            <textarea id="outGoLive" rows="2"></textarea>
            <span class="count" id="outGoLiveCount"></span>
          </label>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Welcome message (TTS-safe)</span>
            <textarea id="outWelcome" rows="3"></textarea>
            <span class="count" id="outWelcomeCount"></span>
          </label>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Discord post</span>
            <textarea id="outDiscord" rows="5"></textarea>
          </label>

          <div class="row">
            <button class="btn amber" id="csExport">Export stream-config.json</button>
            <button class="btn secondary" id="csCopyAll">Copy Discord post</button>
          </div>
          <p class="note">Export carries exactly the five keys the Mochi stream stack consumes at startup: twitchTitle, twitchCategory, goLiveMessage, welcomeMessage, discordMessage.</p>
          <p class="error-text" id="csErrors"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ MOCHI & SESSIONS ============ -->
    <section class="module" id="module-mochi">
      <div class="grid two">
        <div class="card">
          <h2>Host profiles</h2>
          <p class="lede">A host profile is one Mochi bridge: label, bridge base URL, bridge token. Switching the active profile is how Mochi's hosting location changes — NeoDerrp PC today, derrp-server later. Profiles and tokens live only in this browser.</p>

          <label class="field">
            <span>Active host</span>
            <select id="hostActive"></select>
          </label>
          <div class="row">
            <span class="chip" id="bridgeStateChip"><span class="dot"></span><span id="bridgeStateText">Bridge not connected</span></span>
            <button class="btn small" id="bridgeCheck">Check connection</button>
            <button class="btn small secondary" id="bridgeRefresh">Refresh status</button>
          </div>
          <p class="note" id="bridgeDetail">No host profile configured yet. Add one below to connect to a bridge.</p>

          <h3>Add / edit profile</h3>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Label</span>
            <input type="text" id="hostLabel" placeholder="e.g. NeoDerrp (PC)" />
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Bridge base URL (tailnet HTTPS address)</span>
            <input type="url" id="hostUrl" placeholder="https://your-pc.your-tailnet.ts.net" />
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Bridge token</span>
            <input type="password" id="hostToken" placeholder="Bridge bearer token (never a stack token)" autocomplete="off" />
          </label>
          <div class="row">
            <button class="btn" id="hostSave">Save profile</button>
            <button class="btn danger" id="hostDelete">Delete active profile</button>
          </div>
          <p class="note">The Studio holds only the bridge's own token. Stack credentials never leave the PC — the bridge injects them itself.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>Mochi stack</h2>
          <p class="lede">Component status comes from the bridge (<code>GET /status</code>) when connected. Without a bridge, status is honestly unknown — never guessed.</p>
          <div class="stack-grid" id="stackGrid"></div>
          <p class="note" id="sessionBridgeNote">Session state from the bridge (<code>GET /session</code>) will appear here when connected.</p>
          <div class="output-box" id="sessionBridgeBox">Bridge not connected — no live session state available.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <div class="row" style="justify-content:space-between;">
          <h2>Launchpad</h2>
          <div class="row">
            <span class="chip" id="launchpadLockChip"><span class="dot"></span><span id="launchpadLockText">Bridge not connected</span></span>
            <button class="btn small secondary" id="launchpadRefresh" disabled>Refresh launchers</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">Allowlisted household stacks served by the active host profile's bridge (<code>GET /launchers</code>). Only entries marked launchable by the bridge render Launch / Stop buttons; all other entries display their status and registry state honestly.</p>
        <p class="note" id="launchpadState">Connect a bridge to load the launcher registry.</p>
        <div class="launchpad-grid" id="launchpadGrid"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <h2>Config files</h2>
        <p class="lede">Allowlisted configs the bridge serves: <code>stream-config.json</code>, Mochi personality / profile prompt files, and AI-Mochi vault files. Writes go through the bridge only — backup-first, validated, and revertible — and stay disabled until the bridge reports live control.</p>
        <div class="row">
          <button class="btn secondary" id="cfgLoad" disabled>Load config list from bridge</button>
          <span class="note" id="cfgState">Connect a bridge to browse config files.</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="list" id="cfgList"></ul>
        <label class="field">
          <span>File contents</span>
          <textarea id="cfgContent" rows="10" placeholder="Select a config file to view it here." disabled></textarea>
        </label>
        <div class="row">
          <button class="btn" id="cfgSave" disabled>Save via bridge (backup-first)</button>
          <button class="btn secondary" id="cfgRevert" disabled>Revert last write</button>
          <span class="note" id="cfgLockNote">Editing is locked: writes require a connected bridge with control unlocked.</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <h2>Sessions</h2>
        <p class="lede">The nine-stage lifecycle, tracked locally. When the bridge is connected, live session state shows above; this checklist stays manual either way, so the Studio is useful with the bridge off.</p>
        <div class="row">
          <input type="text" id="sessName" class="grow" placeholder="Session name (e.g. Main Quest Monday — Metaphor)" />
          <button class="btn" id="sessCreate">New session</button>
          <select id="sessActive" class="grow"></select>
          <button class="btn danger" id="sessDelete">Delete session</button>
        </div>
        <ol class="stage-list" id="stageList" style="margin-top:0.8rem;"></ol>
        <label class="field">
          <span>Post-stream review notes</span>
          <textarea id="sessNotes" rows="4" placeholder="What worked, what broke, what to change next time…"></textarea>
        </label>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ WEEK PLANNER ============ -->
    <section class="module" id="module-planner">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Household week</h2>
        <p class="lede" id="plannerRange">The ruled Mon–Sun pattern, pre-filled on real dates. Saturday is family day: scheduling anything there requires a typed override note — no exceptions.</p>
        <div class="week-grid" id="weekGrid"></div>
        <p class="error-text" id="plannerError"></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ QUEUE & PROMPTS ============ -->
    <section class="module" id="module-queue">
      <div class="grid two">
        <div class="card">
          <h2>Request queue</h2>
          <p class="lede">Ama's commission &amp; drawing-request queue. Requester names are hidden by default — anonymous-by-default, on purpose.</p>
          <label class="switch">
            <input type="checkbox" id="queueAnon" checked />
            Anonymous by default (hide requester names)
          </label>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top:0.6rem;">
            <input type="text" id="qRequester" class="grow" placeholder="Requester (kept private when anonymous)" />
            <input type="text" id="qItem" class="grow" placeholder="Request (e.g. coloured doodle of my OC)" />
            <button class="btn" id="qAdd">Add</button>
          </div>
          <ul class="list" id="qList"></ul>

          <h3>Reference — bits &amp; subs</h3>
          <ul class="list">
            <li><span class="grow">Bits 100</span><span class="meta">derp doodle</span></li>
            <li><span class="grow">Bits 500</span><span class="meta">coloured doodle</span></li>
            <li><span class="grow">Bits 1,000</span><span class="meta">full piece</span></li>
            <li><span class="grow">Sub T1</span><span class="meta">Derpling</span></li>
            <li><span class="grow">Sub T2</span><span class="meta">Cryptid — priority requests</span></li>
            <li><span class="grow">Sub T3</span><span class="meta">Cryptid + raffle entry</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>Prompt Jar</h2>
          <p class="lede">Drop in drawing prompts; pull one at random when the jar gets shaken on stream.</p>
          <div class="row">
            <input type="text" id="jarInput" class="grow" placeholder="New prompt…" />
            <button class="btn" id="jarAdd">Add prompt</button>
            <button class="btn amber" id="jarDraw">Draw one</button>
          </div>
          <div class="output-box" id="jarResult" style="margin-top:0.7rem;">The jar is waiting.</div>
          <ul class="list" id="jarList"></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ COMMISSION PREP ============ -->
    <section class="module" id="module-commissions">
      <div class="grid two">
        <div class="card">
          <h2>Commission Prep</h2>
          <p class="lede">Prep sheet for Ama's commissions. Client identity stays off the sheet unless you deliberately turn anonymity off.</p>
          <label class="switch">
            <input type="checkbox" id="cpAnon" checked />
            Anonymous prep sheet (hide client name)
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Client name</span>
            <input type="text" id="cpClient" placeholder="Client (hidden while anonymous)" />
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Piece type</span>
            <select id="cpType">
              <option value="headshot">Headshot</option>
              <option value="bust">Bust-up</option>
              <option value="full">Full body</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Subject / character</span>
            <input type="text" id="cpSubject" placeholder="Who or what is being drawn" />
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Details &amp; references</span>
            <textarea id="cpDetails" rows="4" placeholder="Pose, palette, must-haves, reference links the client provided…"></textarea>
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Deadline (optional)</span>
            <input type="text" id="cpDeadline" placeholder="e.g. before Friday's stream" />
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>Pricing &amp; booking</h2>
          <p class="lede">Commissions are booked through VGen only — never by DM. Prices stay link-only unless the price toggle is on.</p>
          <p><a href="https://vgen.co/amaderrp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">vgen.co/amaderrp</a></p>
          <label class="switch">
            <input type="checkbox" id="cpShowPrices" />
            Show prices (default: VGen-link-only)
          </label>
          <div id="cpPrices" style="display:none; margin-top:0.6rem;">
            <ul class="list">
              <li><span class="grow">Headshot</span><span class="meta">from $30</span></li>
              <li><span class="grow">Bust-up</span><span class="meta">from $50</span></li>
              <li><span class="grow">Full body</span><span class="meta">from $80</span></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="note">Commercial licence required for stream/business use.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="note" id="cpPriceNote">Prices hidden — copy points to the VGen page.</p>

          <h3>Prep sheet</h3>
          <div class="output-box" id="cpSheet">Fill in the prep form to generate the sheet.</div>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top:0.6rem;">
            <button class="btn secondary" id="cpCopy">Copy prep sheet</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ PROMO & SOCIAL ============ -->
    <section class="module" id="module-promo">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Promo &amp; Social</h2>
        <p class="lede">Cross-promo variants generated from the current Copy Studio set. Invite fields are editable and stored per browser — the Art Gloop invite is intentionally blank: a previously documented one is invalid, so paste the current invite before posting.</p>
        <div class="grid two">
          <label class="field">
            <span>The Derrps — Discord invite</span>
            <input type="url" id="promoInviteDerrps" value="https://discord.gg/pVPFG475Y7" />
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Art Gloop — Discord invite (no default; paste the current one)</span>
            <input type="url" id="promoInviteGloop" placeholder="Paste the current Art Gloop invite link" />
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <button class="btn" id="promoGenerate">Generate from current copy set</button>
          <span class="note" id="promoState">Uses whatever is currently in Copy Studio.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="grid two" style="margin-top:0.8rem;">
          <div>
            <h3>The Derrps (Discord)</h3>
            <div class="output-box" id="promoDerrps">—</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Art Gloop (Discord)</h3>
            <div class="output-box" id="promoGloop">—</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>YouTube</h3>
            <div class="output-box" id="promoYoutube">—</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Shorts</h3>
            <div class="output-box" id="promoShorts">—</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Instagram</h3>
            <div class="output-box" id="promoInsta">—</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ COMPANION ============ -->
    <section class="module" id="module-companion">
      <div class="grid three">
        <div class="card">
          <h2>Tracker</h2>
          <p class="lede">Cloud Metaphor Companion tracker (Vercel + Supabase) — opens in a new tab.</p>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Tracker URL</span>
            <input type="url" id="compTrackerUrl" placeholder="Paste the current Tracker address" />
          </label>
          <div class="row">
            <button class="btn" id="compTrackerOpen" disabled>Open</button>
            <span class="note" id="compTrackerNote">No address set yet</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>Local / Stream Companion</h2>
          <p class="lede">Local / stream Companion instance running on NeoDerrp during stream sessions.</p>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Local / Stream Companion URL</span>
            <input type="url" id="compLocalUrl" placeholder="Paste the current local Companion address" />
          </label>
          <div class="row">
            <button class="btn" id="compLocalOpen" disabled>Open</button>
            <span class="note" id="compLocalNote">No address set yet</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>OBS Overlay</h2>
          <p class="lede">Stream overlay view for OBS browser sources and pre-flight layout checks.</p>
          <label class="field">
            <span>OBS Overlay URL</span>
            <input type="url" id="compOverlayUrl" placeholder="Paste the current OBS Overlay address" />
          </label>
          <div class="row">
            <button class="btn" id="compOverlayOpen" disabled>Open</button>
            <span class="note" id="compOverlayNote">No address set yet</span>
          </div>

          <h3>OBS overlay helper</h3>
          <div class="output-box" id="compOverlayReadout">No address set yet</div>
          <p class="note" style="margin-top:0.45rem;">Until party data is verified, use the overlay with <code>?panels=enemy,recs</code> (or disable the party panel) — the party block otherwise shows member levels plus the inactive slot.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top:0.45rem;">
            <button class="btn small secondary" id="compOverlayCopySafe" disabled>Copy with ?panels=enemy,recs</button>
            <button class="btn small secondary" id="compOverlayCopyBase" disabled>Copy stored base URL</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid two" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <div class="card">
          <h2>Desktop reader</h2>
          <p class="lede">The desktop reader is a separate read-only Windows app (verified fields only) — it can now be launched from the Launchpad (entry #8), has no stop button (close its window manually when done), and never launches the game.</p>
          <div class="row">
            <button class="btn secondary" disabled>Launch from Launchpad (entry #8)</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>Launch from Studio — not built yet</h2>
          <p class="lede">Bridge Launcher registry slot (Launcher spec entry #4).</p>
          <div class="row">
            <button class="btn" disabled>Launch</button>
            <span class="chip warn"><span class="dot"></span>Not built yet</span>
          </div>
          <p class="note" style="margin-top:0.55rem;">The Companion launcher was spec'd but never built, so this card activates only when that launcher exists and Gate L reaches it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    Derrp Studio — NeoDerrp &amp; AmaDerrp's household command center. Drafts, planner entries, and host profiles are stored locally in this browser; stream control runs only through the Mochi bridge on the tailnet.
  </footer>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/app.js';
  </script>
</Layout>
